      "writtenOn": "2022-07-29T15:47:46Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Weirdly enough, there is neither a requirement to clear on disconnect nor a requirement not to clear on disconnect.  \n\n\u00276.4.3.3.2 BIST Shared Test Mode Exit\u0027 has a lot of very specific conditions where we can\u0027t clear the mode (resets, swaps), and specifically requires that we exit upon receiving our exit message or powering off.  I don\u0027t see any indications of what a disconnect should do. \n\nReading the PD3 CTSr1.4 V4 spec, I can\u0027t find where the tester would ever send us a Shared Mode Test Exit message... I\u0027ll start a thread with the PD WG",
      "parentUuid": "a88b007c_f483f022",
      "revId": "dd956ef781930f900244c31bb54083c58a17e368",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "d439201c_13030234",
        "filename": "common/usbc/usb_pd_dpm.c",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 620,
      "author": {
        "id": 1287197
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-07-29T19:25:49Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Okay, partway through starting the thread I found this tidbit in the CTS PDF:\n\"TEST NOTES:\n* Once the UUT is placed in the test mode it is expected to remain in the test mode till it is\npowered down.\n* The test procedure should be performed only one time per port.\"\n\nSo it implies the condition persists on port disconnect between tests.  The PD spec needs either an ECR or a comments update to align it.",
      "parentUuid": "d7310400_1549ca65",
      "revId": "dd956ef781930f900244c31bb54083c58a17e368",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
