        "id": 1287197
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-07-29T15:47:46Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The CONFIG name isn\u0027t the best at describing it, but at this point it\u0027s basically an indicator for whether a board is using the DPM\u0027s shared power logic.  The boards that disable it are either 1) incapable of sourcing 3.0 A on all ports due to a sub-board connector issue or 2) always sourcing a bunch of power (honeybuns)\n\nSo if a board were to implement their own shared power strategy, we\u0027d need to have them overriding all the relevant dpm_* callbacks",
      "parentUuid": "8c73b4a4_a74b5a69",
      "revId": "dd956ef781930f900244c31bb54083c58a17e368",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
